$$\frac{a}{1 - r} = 15 \quad \text{and} \quad \frac{a^2}{1 - r^2} = 45.$$
We can write $a$ in terms of $r$ using the first equation:
$$a = 15(1 - r),$$
and substitute into the second equation to get
$$\frac{15(1 - r) \times a^2}{1 - r^2} = 45,$$
which simplifies to
$$a^2 + a - 6 = 0.$$
Our quadratic factors as
